# Twice-Told Critiques

Peer reviews from three ML conferences and five open-review journal sources, with claims extracted by an LLM,
problem groups for each paper's reviews, and MELD, EditLens and GPTTrace scores for LLM-generated text. This is the data of the paper
"Twice-Told Critiques: Claim-Level Homogenization of Peer Review in the LLM Era". Code:
https://github.com/IlyaGusev/twicetold.

{{ n_reviews }} reviews, {{ n_papers }} papers, {{ n_panels }} panels.

## Sources

{{ sources }}

- `in_sample`: the review is in an analysis sample (at most 5 reviews per paper, sampled papers only).
- `with_claims`: the review has extracted claims.
- `with_meld`: the review has a MELD score.
- `with_editlens`: the review has an EditLens score.
- `with_gpttrace`: the review has a GPTTrace score.

Conference reviews: ICLR and NeurIPS from OpenReview via
[ResearchArcade](https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulab-ai/ResearchArcade-openreview-reviews) and
[iclr-2026](https://huggingface.co/datasets/davidheineman/iclr-2026); ICML 2025–2026 accepted papers and ICLR
2027 submissions from the OpenReview API. ICLR 2027 reviews were downloaded on 15 November 2026, after the first
author responses and before decisions. Journal reports: SciPost (API); F1000Research, Wellcome Open Research, Open Research Europe and PLOS
(Europe PMC); BMC Medicine ([JerMa88/BMC_Medicine_Peer_Reviews](https://huggingface.co/datasets/JerMa88/BMC_Medicine_Peer_Reviews));
Copernicus/EGU (journal discussion pages). Journal samples hold up to 2,000 papers per source-year, first-round
reports only.

## Configs

### `reviews`

One row per review. One file per source.

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `source` | `ICLR`, `NeurIPS`, `ICML`, `BMC-Med`, `Copernicus`, `F1000`, `PLOS`, `SciPost` |
| `venue_type` | `conference` or `journal` |
| `journal`, `field` | Journal name and field |
| `year`, `paper_id`, `review_id` | Source year and source ids |
| `reviewer` | Anonymous label such as `Reviewer 2` or `Reviewer_8LjP`; null when the source gives none |
| `rating`, `rating_raw` | Numeric rating where the source has one, and the source label |
| `confidence` | Reviewer confidence (conferences) |
| `text` | Review text; conference form fields are joined with `[FIELD]` headers |
| `form` | Conference review form fields |
| `review_time` | Review date (UTC) |
| `withdrawn`, `decision` | Paper status (conferences); `decision` is `pending` for ICLR 2027 papers under review |
| `licence` | Licence of the text |
| `in_corpus` | The review is in the current corpus; `false` for 414 early ICLR sample reviews that a later corpus build dropped |
| `corpus_row` | Row order in the corpus files of the code repository |
| `sample`, `sample_row` | Analysis sample (`main`: ICLR and NeurIPS, `icml`, `journal`) and row order in it |
| `claims` | Extracted claims: list of `{claim, quote, category, target, specific}`; empty list when the review has no critique; null when not extracted |
| `claims_error` | API error when extraction failed after four attempts |
| `meld_score` | MELD score: mean of the top token scores |
| `meld_tokens` | Number of scored tokens |
| `meld_family`, `meld_task` | MELD's most likely LLM family and operation (for example `generate` or `polish`) |
| `meld_flag` | `meld_score` is above the threshold |
| `meld_written` | `meld_flag` and `meld_task == "generate"` |
| `editlens_score` | EditLens score of the first {{ editlens_max_length }} tokens, from 0 (human) to 1 (LLM-written) |
| `editlens_tokens` | Number of tokens of the whole text |
| `editlens_flag` | `editlens_score` is above the threshold |
| `gpttrace_score` | GPTTrace score of the first {{ gpttrace_max_length }} tokens: logit of machine-generated minus logit of human |
| `gpttrace_score_mean` | Token-weighted mean of the GPTTrace scores of all {{ gpttrace_max_length }}-token windows of the text |
| `gpttrace_tokens` | Number of tokens of the whole text |
| `gpttrace_flag` | `gpttrace_score` is above the threshold |

### `papers`

One row per paper with at least one review in `reviews`: title, abstract (conferences), decision, withdrawn
status, OpenReview primary area, predicted area (`area_pred`, ICLR and NeurIPS sample papers), licence and number of
reviews.

### `panels`

One row per panel: a set of reviews whose claims the LLM grouped into shared problems.

{{ panels }}

- `paper`: the reviews of one ICLR or NeurIPS paper (main analysis). ICLR 2026 and 2027 hold all papers with three or more
  reviews, withdrawn and desk-rejected papers included.
- `icml`, `journal`: the reviews of one ICML or journal paper.
- `subset3`: three-review subsets of papers with at least four reviews.
- `noq`, `nocq`: the same papers with review variants from the `variants` config.
- `placebo_venue`, `placebo_area`, `journal_placebo`: one review each from different papers of one venue-year (or
  one predicted area-year). Overlap here measures matches that do not come from a shared paper.

Columns: `panel_id`, `kind`, `review_ids`, `targets` (list of `{target_id, element}`), `clusters` (list of
`{target_id, problem, claim_ids}`), `error` (API error; then `targets` and `clusters` are null). The table above
counts panels without errors. A claim id `R{i}-{j}` is claim `j` of review `review_ids[i]`, in the order of
the `claims` column.

### `variants`

Review texts with one field removed, for robustness checks: `noq` without the questions field, `nocq` (ICLR 2023)
without the clarity field. Columns: `variant`, `review_id` (with the variant prefix), `base_review_id`, `source`,
`year`, `paper_id`, `text`, `sample_row`, `claims`, `claims_error`.

## Folders

| Folder | Content |
|---|---|
| `final/` | The four configs above: `reviews`, `papers`, `panels`, `variants`. The paper's analysis reads only this folder, `gold/` and `additional/` |
| `gold/` | Reference annotations of the extraction and grouping checks, and the two external human benchmarks |
| `additional/` | Side experiments: the rewrite test, LLM reviews of arXiv papers, the known-origin texts of the detector checks, and Gemini Embedding 2 vectors (1,536 dimensions) of the first 20,000 characters of each `main` sample review, in `sample_row` order |
| `raw/` | Inputs of the corpus build: OpenReview API dumps of ICML 2025 and 2026 accepted papers and all ICLR 2027 submissions, predicted research areas, journal fetch statistics, the panel files and the MELD, EditLens and GPTTrace scores of all scored texts |

`python src/release.py pull` copies `final/`, `gold/` and `additional/` into `data/`; `--raw` adds `raw/`.

## Extraction

Model: `{{ model }}` (OpenRouter route `{{ route }}`), reasoning effort `{{ efforts.pass1 }}` for claims and
`{{ efforts.pass2 }}` for grouping. Prompts: `src/prompts/pass1.j2` and `src/prompts/pass2.j2` in the code repository.
The model sees each review in full.

## MELD

Detector: [{{ meld_repo }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ meld_repo }}), revision `{{ meld_revision }}`. Threshold
{{ threshold }}: the {{ quantile }} quantile of scores on {{ calibration_reviews }} reviews from {{ calibration_last_year }} and
earlier. So about 0.1% of human-written reviews carry `meld_flag`. A flag is a detector output, not proof that a
reviewer used an LLM. Do not use it to judge an individual reviewer.

## EditLens

Detector: [{{ editlens_repo }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ editlens_repo }}), revision `{{ editlens_revision }}`, a LoRA
adapter on Llama-3.2-3B (loaded from `{{ editlens_base_repo }}` in 4 bits). The score covers the first
{{ editlens_max_length }} tokens of a text, as in Pangram's inference script. Threshold {{ editlens_threshold }}: the same
quantile of the same reviews as for MELD. `raw/editlens_scores.jsonl` also holds the token-weighted mean score over
all windows of a text. The same warning applies: a flag is a detector output.

## GPTTrace

Detector: [{{ gpttrace_repo }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ gpttrace_repo }}), revision `{{ gpttrace_revision }}`, a
binary classifier on the Ettin 1B encoder. Its author trained it on the first {{ gpttrace_max_length }} tokens of each
text, so `gpttrace_score` covers the first {{ gpttrace_max_length }} tokens. Threshold {{ gpttrace_threshold }}: the
same quantile of the same reviews as for MELD. The paper does not use these scores. The same warning applies: a flag
is a detector output.

